
# Task05 – Static Members and Arrays of Objects

## Aim
To understand static data members, static member functions,
constructors and arrays of objects in C++.

## Concepts Used

1. Static data members
2. Static member functions
3. Constructor
4. Arrays of objects
5. Accessing shared class data
6. Scope resolution operator

## Explanation

A static data member belongs to the entire class rather than
to an individual object. Only one copy is shared by all objects.

In the Token class, the static variable next starts at 100.
Every constructor call increments it.

Three Token objects are created in the array and one extra
Token object is created. Therefore, the constructor runs
four times.

The IDs are 101, 102, 103 and 104.

The output is:
101 103 104 4

The static variable is defined outside the class using:

int Token::next = 100;

